#                        set a battle writes back troop counts and wounded only (a wiped troop
#                        leaves); hero buffs stay in the battle (generic.hpp apply_battle_army,
#                        all formats). SLG_A_FULL=1 restores the buff write-back as a report-only
#                        stress variant. Default mode unchanged (same digests and report sums).
#   2026-11-03 viewport cases redefined (susu 07:22Z, thread 整理与竞品的性能对比): no 3x3
#                        block window; a client holds exactly its 512x384 viewport (tiles of
#                        32 px with terrain/level/owner, units, march lines crossing it). EB
#                        browse (class 2): every client drags or jumps its view every tick and
#                        pulls the whole viewport. UP/UC/US static (class 3): clients stay put
#                        and get one delta per tick of the changes inside their viewport; NP/NC/NS
#                        native with one baseline per client; K* removed. ViewSnapshot/ViewDelta
#                        gain a tiles list in every model, adapter and schema (schema names v3).
#                        Default mode unchanged (same digests and report sums). After the
#                        untimed first pull every static client reserves 1.5x + 16 unit and march
#                        slots in its held view (all formats). Native views: one slot-class buffer
#                        per client, every change touched, deltas with touched_only. EB.send excludes
#                        the spatial query (units_in / marches_in), untimed bookkeeping like U*'s tracker.
#   2026-11-03 realistic map unit (susu 08:54Z): ViewUnit has 40 fields (33 scalars, three
#                        strings, nested UnitHero commander, hero/troop/buff lists) in every model,
#                        adapter and schema (schema names v4); world events change several fields
#                        each; held views up to SLOT_MAX. Default mode unchanged.
#   2026-11-03 EBW.recv (report column, thread 优化客户端视口同步性能): each EB pull is also
#                        received into one extra held view (index clients) reused by every pull,
#                        the warm single-device receive; must read the same as the client's view.
#                        EB keys and numbers unchanged; class 3 unchanged.
